# Customer source files - never commit
inputs/

# Backups of customer workbooks - same policy as inputs/ (R-P89). R-P78 requires
# the write-back backups be kept, so exclusion is the only available fix: each
# .bak.xlsx is a byte-identical copy of the customer workbook, and the
# delivery-target backup is a copy of what sat in the customer review folder.
backup/

# Regenerable artifacts (rebuilt by the Step 1 scripts). Add this feature's
# own data/*.json artefacts here as Step 1 starts emitting them.
data/recon.json
lint_report.json

# batches/ is excluded, and not because it is regenerable — re-running the
# Step 2 scripts does not reproduce the verdicts. It is excluded because each
# row embeds the workbook's Pre-conditions and Test Procedure text verbatim as
# a before/after pair, which is the same content the root-level output/ rule
# and inputs/ keep out. The audit value lives in _meta plus the row / tc_id /
# changed fields; emitting those without the prose is the fix if the trail
# ever needs to be tracked.
batches/

# Carry customer prose rather than derived structure — same policy as inputs/.
# sysad_sections.json bleeds SYSAD paragraph body text into its heading field;
# the er_* pair embeds the workbook's Expected Result / Procedure text verbatim.
data/sysad_sections.json
data/er_divergence.json
data/er_narrow_gate.log.json
data/remarks_scope_gate.log.json

# PCTS Verifier uiautomator dumps ARE tracked (R-P90). The earlier exclusion
# asked the wrong question: not "can this KIND of data be produced again" but
# "can the OBSERVATION that produced it be reproduced". R-P11 binds L-PJ7 to one
# specific combination - Pixel 10 / Android 16 / PCTS Verifier
# 5.1-prod.922397802 - which may not survive device retirement, an OS upgrade,
# or the apk version being pulled. L-PJ7 reads pcts_evidence.json's status to
# decide whether 23 rows may be edited; if that status is ever challenged, these
# dumps are the only physical evidence.
#   Evidence is valuable because it records a moment, not because it records a
#   kind of fact.
# 14 files, 297 KB, no workbook prose (verified: 0 verbatim fragments).

# The remaining data/*_sections.json ARE tracked on purpose (as Home's
# spec_id_to_outline.tsv and sxm/amfm's stla_to_cfts.tsv are): they are the
# traceability lookups every spec_reference is linted against, they carry ids
# and heading names rather than requirement text, and a diff on one is the
# signal that the spec export moved underneath us.

# Local noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
output/
.DS_Store
